{"book":16,"chapter":13,"rubric":"FROM ASSEMBLER TO C / GOING DEEPER / CHAPTER 13","slides":[{"title":"What a test is","sub":"Chapter 13 · a program with an exit code","short":"Test","main":"A test calls the code and returns a nonzero code on mismatch.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["A program with an exit code","Tests are documentation","Next to the code"],"captions":["A test is a program that calls the code with a known input, compares the result with the expected one, and returns a nonzero code on mismatch","A test suite shows how a function should behave on ordinary and edge data","Tests live next to the code and run on every change: make test → exit 0 or not 0"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int main(void) {","    if (add(2, 3) != 5) return 1;","    return 0;","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"add(2, 3) == 5","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"add(INT_MAX, 1) → error","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"add(0, 0) == 0","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"text":"behavior\ndocumented","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["project/","  src/  tests/  Makefile","$ make test      # exit 0 — all good"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[17.8,31.0]}]},{"title":"assert and errors","sub":"Contracts","short":"assert","main":"assert is for program bugs, error codes are for bad input.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Contract and error","Pre-, post-, invariant","NDEBUG"],"captions":["assert guards the contract between parts of a program (the caller broke it — that is a bug); invalid user input is a normal case, so return an error code","The callee checks preconditions, it guarantees postconditions itself, structure invariants hold between operations","-DNDEBUG disables assert in release: the condition must have no side effects"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"program bug → assert","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":104.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"bad input → error code","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":82.0,"text":"different\nclasses","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int pop(struct stack *s) {","    assert(s && s->n > 0);        // pre","    int v = s->a[--s->n];","    assert(s->n < s->cap);        // invariant","    return v;","}"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["assert(i++ < n);   // ✕ side effect","assert(i < n); i++;"],"hl":[1],"bad":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[17.1,24.9]}]},{"title":"Minimal framework","sub":"EXPECT macros","short":"Framework","main":"File, line, expression, both values; the result is the exit code.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Macros","Registration and summary","Ready-made libraries"],"captions":["TEST defines a function, EXPECT_EQ compares values and on failure prints file, line, expression and both values — without aborting the test","The runner walks the table of tests, prints a summary and returns a nonzero code on any failure","Unity, Check, cmocka do the same with more comfort: one principle — an ordinary program and an exit code"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#define EXPECT_EQ(a, b) do {                 \\","    long long _x = (a), _y = (b);             \\","    if (_x != _y) fail(__FILE__, __LINE__,   \\","                       #a \" == \" #b, _x, _y);  \\","} while (0)"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"c","size":8.0,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["static const struct test tests[] = {","    {\"add\", test_add}, {\"sub\", test_sub},","};","return failed ? 1 : 0;"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Unity","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Check","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"cmocka","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.8,30.1]}]},{"title":"What to test","sub":"Boundaries and classes","short":"What","main":"Boundaries, equivalence classes, case tables.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Boundaries","Equivalence classes","Case table"],"captions":["Empty input, one element, minimum, maximum, values one below and one above each boundary","One representative per group of inputs the code handles the same way; errors separately: NULL, small buffer, bad format","Write cases as a table: an array of {input, expected} and one loop — adding a case means adding a line"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":50.0,"y":70.0,"w":48.0,"h":28.0,"text":"-1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":104.0,"y":70.0,"w":48.0,"h":28.0,"text":"0","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":158.0,"y":70.0,"w":48.0,"h":28.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":212.0,"y":70.0,"w":48.0,"h":28.0,"text":"99","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b4","x":266.0,"y":70.0,"w":48.0,"h":28.0,"text":"100","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b5","x":320.0,"y":70.0,"w":48.0,"h":28.0,"text":"101","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"range edge [0, 100]","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"negative → error","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"0…100 → result",