ng allocator tests the error path.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Kinds of doubles","Failing allocator","What we check"],"captions":["A stub returns canned values; a fake is a simplified working implementation; a spy records calls; a mock declares the expected calls up front","An allocator failing on the n-th call checks that on out-of-memory the function frees everything it allocated","Run with a failure at every allocation in turn: no leaks, an error code returned, the structure intact"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"stub","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"fake","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"spy","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":190.0,"y":90.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"mock","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["void *fail_nth(size_t n) {","    return ++calls == fail_at ? NULL","                              : malloc(n);","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["for (int k = 1; k <= allocs; k++) {","    fail_at = k;","    int rc = build(…);","    assert(rc != 0 && live_blocks == 0);","}"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":345.0}]],"cues":[17.2,23.2]}]},{"title":"Coverage and mutations","sub":"gcov","short":"Coverage","main":"Coverage is a hint, not a quality measure.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["gcov","Coverage ≠ quality","Mutations"],"captions":["-fprofile-arcs -ftest-coverage inserts counters, gcov shows the lines and branches the tests never reached","A test with no checks covers the code fully and proves nothing","Mutation testing breaks the code (< to <=) and sees whether tests notice: if not, the test is weak"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["    5:  int f(int x) {","    5:      if (x > 0)","    3:          return 1;","#####:      return -1;","    5:  }"],"hl":[3],"bad":[3],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["void test(void) {","    f(5);       // called but not checked","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"100% coverage, 0 checks","tone":"red","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["if (x < n)    →    if (x <= n)","tests green?  mutant survived — test is weak"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":30.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[15.4,24.6]}]},{"title":"Properties and fuzzing","sub":"Laws instead of examples","short":"Properties","main":"Deterministic generator, shrinking, fuzzing.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Properties","Shrinking","Fuzzing"],"captions":["A law instead of an example: decode(encode(x)) == x, sort is idempotent; a deterministic generator and printing the seed on failure","A large failing input is shrunk: chunks are removed while the property still fails — a minimal example remains","Fuzzing: a mutator corrupts inputs, sanitizers catch crashes; found inputs go to the corpus and to regression tests"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {","    gen(buf, &len, seed + i);","    assert(decode(encode(buf, len)) == buf);","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"1000 B","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"40 B","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":300.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"3 B","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":220.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":260.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"mutator","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"target + ASan","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"corpus","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":250.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":270.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[16.2,25.4]}]},{"title":"Regressions and CI","sub":"Configuration matrix","short":"CI","main":"Every bug becomes a test; run in several configurations.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Bug → test","Continuous integration","Configuration matrix"],"captions":["Every bug found becomes a regression test: first it reproduces the bug, then it stays forever","Tests run automatically on the server at every change: continuous integration","Matrix: -O0 and -O2, gcc and clang, ASan and UBSan separately — much UB shows up in only one configuration"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"bug","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"test","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"forever","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":110.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":150.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":230.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":270.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"commit","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"build","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h"